---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="Services — LucrumTech"
  description="Strategy, engineering, AI and technical leadership under one accountable team — not four vendors with four contracts and nobody answering for the result."
>
  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Services</p>
      <h1>Everything it takes to own a product — under one accountable team.</h1>
      <p class="lede" style="margin-top:24px">Strategy, engineering, AI and technical leadership. Not four vendors with four contracts and nobody answering for the result.</p>
      <div class="grid2">
        <div class="blk"><h3>Product strategy</h3><p>We define what to build before a single line of code is written.</p><ul><li>Market validation and problem definition</li><li>Roadmap and release sequencing</li><li>System architecture design</li><li>Technology selection, trade-offs written down</li></ul></div>
        <div class="blk"><h3>Engineering</h3><p>A delivery team we built and trained ourselves, led by people who have shipped before.</p><ul><li>Full-stack product development</li><li>Cloud infrastructure and platform engineering</li><li>Enterprise platforms and integrations</li><li>Industrial and embedded software, IoT</li></ul></div>
        <div class="blk"><h3>AI transformation</h3><p>AI where it creates real value — built for production, not demos.</p><ul><li>Document intelligence at volume</li><li>Workflow automation with AI decision layers</li><li>Predictive analytics on operational data</li><li>Copilots embedded inside the workflow</li><li>AI optimisation of processes you already run</li></ul></div>
        <div class="blk"><h3>Technical leadership</h3><p>Executive-level technology leadership without the full-time overhead.</p><ul><li>Fractional CTO</li><li>Product management and delivery ownership</li><li>Architectural decisions and technical due diligence</li><li>Vendor and team assessment</li></ul></div>
      </div>
      <p class="sub" style="margin-top:34px">Deepest experience: manufacturing and industrial automation, insurance and FinTech, HealthTech. Also shipped in SaaS, AdTech, Telecom, IoT and embedded systems.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="tint">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">How we charge</p>
      <h2>Two ways to work. We'll tell you which one you need.</h2>
      <div class="grid2">
        <div class="blk"><h3>Leadership advisory</h3><p>Direct time with the three of us — product and delivery, organisation, hiring. For a specific question, a decision you need a second opinion on, or a short review. Billed hourly, no commitment, no minimum.</p><ul><li>Architecture and technology reviews</li><li>Product and roadmap decisions</li><li>Vendor or team assessment</li></ul></div>
        <div class="blk"><h3>Package — three to six months</h3><p>For work that needs owning rather than advising. One price covering the audit, the plan and the execution — leadership and delivery team included, not billed by the hour.</p><ul><li>Full audit of what exists today</li><li>Strategy, architecture and organisational plan</li><li>Execution — build, restructure, hire</li><li>Our delivery team included in the price</li><li>One accountable team throughout</li></ul></div>
      </div>
      <p class="sub" style="margin-top:26px">Most engagements start with a paid short review. By the end of it we'll both know whether the package is the right call.</p>
      <div class="btnrow"><a class="btn" href="/contact">Book a strategy call</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
